<title>USA: Georgia Power Vogtle unit resumes production.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power Vogtle unit resumes production.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co's 1,162 megawatt Vogtle nuclear power unit 2 resumed electricity production Saturday from a scheduled maintenance and refueling outage which began October 8, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The Waynesboro, Ga., unit was producing at near 60 percent of capacity early Monday and was expected to reach full output this week, the spokeswoman said Monday.</p>
<p>Vogtle unit 1, also with a capacity of 1,162 megawatts at Waynesboro, was operating normally at full capacity, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a unit of Southern Co.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
